{"route":"/docs/6.0/components/nav/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Nav","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Add lists of links to your pages with various navigation components—tabs, pills, underline—and plenty of options to customize."},"blocks":[{"id":"base-nav","type":"heading","en":"Base nav","level":2},{"id":"base-nav--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Navigation available in Bootstrap share general markup and styles, from the base <code>.nav</code> class to the active and disabled states. Swap modifier classes to switch between each style."},{"id":"base-nav--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The base <code>.nav</code> component is built with flexbox and provides a strong foundation for building all types of navigation components. It includes some style overrides (for working with lists), some link padding for larger hit areas, and basic disabled styling."},{"id":"base-nav--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"base-nav--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"To convey the active state to assistive technologies, use the <code>aria-current</code> attribute — using the <code>page</code> value for current page, or <code>true</code> for the current item in a set."}]},{"id":"base-nav--example-1","type":"demo","key":"005c671d6cae866c649c","height":147},{"id":"base-nav--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"base-nav--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Classes are used throughout, so your markup can be super flexible. Use <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>s like above, <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code> if the order of your items is important, or roll your own with a <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> element. Because the <code>.nav</code> uses <code>display: flex</code>, the nav links behave the same as nav items would, but without the extra markup."},{"id":"base-nav--example-2","type":"demo","key":"96c9495ecd2497bc9477","height":147},{"id":"base-nav--code-2","type":"code","value":"<nav class=\"nav\">\n  <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n</nav>","language":""},{"id":"base-nav--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Where appropriate, you can also use <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> elements instead of <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> elements for the nav links. You can even mix and match—for example, by using buttons for menus."},{"id":"base-nav--example-3","type":"demo","key":"c96c620591d10b5ccf71","height":147},{"id":"base-nav--code-3","type":"code","value":"<nav class=\"nav\">\n  <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <button class=\"nav-link\" data-bs-toggle=\"menu\" href=\"#\" role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Menu</button>\n  <div class=\"menu\">\n    <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Action</a>\n    <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Another action</a>\n    <hr class=\"menu-divider\">\n    <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Something else here</a>\n  </div>\n  <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n</nav>","language":""},{"id":"tab-javascript-plugin","type":"heading","en":"Tab JavaScript plugin","level":2},{"id":"tab-javascript-plugin--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/components/tab#javascript-behavior\">tab JavaScript plugin</a> to create tabbable regions."},{"id":"available-styles","type":"heading","en":"Available styles","level":2},{"id":"available-styles--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Change the style of <code>.nav</code>s component with modifiers and utilities. Mix and match as needed, or build your own."},{"id":"tabs","type":"heading","en":"Tabs","level":3},{"id":"tabs--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Takes the basic nav from above and adds the <code>.nav-tabs</code> class to generate a tabbed interface."},{"id":"tabs--example-1","type":"demo","key":"f763084cc384839163ad","height":147},{"id":"tabs--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"pills","type":"heading","en":"Pills","level":3},{"id":"pills--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Take that same HTML, but use <code>.nav-pills</code> instead for a more themed appearance."},{"id":"pills--example-1","type":"demo","key":"dd528a120171e15bbc97","height":147},{"id":"pills--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-pills\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"pills--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Pill navigation can also go vertical with an additional modifier class, <code>.nav-pills-vertical</code>."},{"id":"pills--example-2","type":"demo","key":"dad045ea10170bcd940c","height":147},{"id":"pills--code-2","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-pills nav-pills-vertical\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"underline","type":"heading","en":"Underline","level":3},{"id":"underline--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Take that same HTML, but use <code>.nav-underline</code> instead:"},{"id":"underline--example-1","type":"demo","key":"3f0b12b512f1501a3b87","height":147},{"id":"underline--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-underline\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"alignment","type":"heading","en":"Alignment","level":2},{"id":"alignment--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Change the alignment of your nav with <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/flex\">flexbox utilities</a>. By default, navs are horizontal and left-aligned, but you can easily modify them to center or right-aligned, and even stacked vertically."},{"id":"horizontal","type":"heading","en":"Horizontal","level":3},{"id":"horizontal--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Centered with <code>.justify-content-center</code>:"},{"id":"horizontal--example-1","type":"demo","key":"de2a48afc93e8e466637","height":147},{"id":"horizontal--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav justify-content-center\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"horizontal--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Right-aligned with <code>.justify-content-end</code>:"},{"id":"horizontal--example-2","type":"demo","key":"537d3bfb9505b011ddb0","height":147},{"id":"horizontal--code-2","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav justify-content-end\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"vertical","type":"heading","en":"Vertical","level":3},{"id":"vertical--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Stack your navigation by changing the flex item direction with the <code>.flex-column</code> utility. Need to stack them on some viewports but not others? Use the responsive versions (e.g., <code>.sm:flex-column</code>)."},{"id":"vertical--example-1","type":"demo","key":"182550319779ed7aa9b6","height":147},{"id":"vertical--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav flex-column\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"vertical--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"As always, vertical navigation is possible without <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>s, too."},{"id":"vertical--example-2","type":"demo","key":"898be9f16cc901919089","height":147},{"id":"vertical--code-2","type":"code","value":"<nav class=\"nav flex-column\">\n  <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n</nav>","language":""},{"id":"fill-and-justify","type":"heading","en":"Fill and justify","level":3},{"id":"fill-and-justify--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Force your <code>.nav</code>’s contents to extend the full available width with one of two modifier classes. To proportionately fill all available space with your <code>.nav-item</code>s, use <code>.nav-fill</code>. Notice that all horizontal space is occupied, but not every nav item has the same width."},{"id":"fill-and-justify--example-1","type":"demo","key":"24abc9b8d8021cf70b06","height":147},{"id":"fill-and-justify--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-pills nav-fill\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Much longer nav link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"fill-and-justify--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"When using a <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>-based navigation, you can safely omit <code>.nav-item</code> as only <code>.nav-link</code> is required for styling <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> elements."},{"id":"fill-and-justify--example-2","type":"demo","key":"81e6e6626125133d0d4d","height":147},{"id":"fill-and-justify--code-2","type":"code","value":"<nav class=\"nav nav-pills nav-fill\">\n  <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Much longer nav link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n</nav>","language":""},{"id":"fill-and-justify--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"For equal-width elements, use <code>.nav-justified</code>. All horizontal space will be occupied by nav links, but unlike the <code>.nav-fill</code> above, every nav item will be the same width."},{"id":"fill-and-justify--example-3","type":"demo","key":"25b81c7e962b70b35d08","height":147},{"id":"fill-and-justify--code-3","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-pills nav-justified\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Much longer nav link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"fill-and-justify--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Similar to the <code>.nav-fill</code> example using a <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>-based navigation."},{"id":"fill-and-justify--example-4","type":"demo","key":"11fde70f47682820144e","height":147},{"id":"fill-and-justify--code-4","type":"code","value":"<nav class=\"nav nav-pills nav-justified\">\n  <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Much longer nav link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n</nav>","language":""},{"id":"working-with-flex-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Working with flex utilities","level":2},{"id":"working-with-flex-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"If you need responsive nav variations, consider using a series of <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/flex\">flexbox utilities</a>. While more verbose, these utilities offer greater customization across responsive breakpoints. In the example below, our nav will be stacked on the lowest breakpoint, then adapt to a horizontal layout that fills the available width starting from the small breakpoint."},{"id":"working-with-flex-utilities--example-1","type":"demo","key":"087bad2cc4d6a24b6f48","height":147},{"id":"working-with-flex-utilities--code-1","type":"code","value":"<nav class=\"nav nav-pills flex-column sm:flex-row\">\n  <a class=\"sm:flex-fill sm:text-center nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  <a class=\"sm:flex-fill sm:text-center nav-link\" href=\"#\">Longer nav link</a>\n  <a class=\"sm:flex-fill sm:text-center nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  <a class=\"sm:flex-fill sm:text-center nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n</nav>","language":""},{"id":"regarding-accessibility","type":"heading","en":"Regarding accessibility","level":2},{"id":"regarding-accessibility--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"If you’re using navs to provide a navigation bar, be sure to add a <code>role=&quot;navigation&quot;</code> to the most logical parent container of the <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>, or wrap a <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> element around the whole navigation. Do not add the role to the <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> itself, as this would prevent it from being announced as an actual list by assistive technologies."},{"id":"regarding-accessibility--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Note that navigation bars, even if visually styled as tabs with the <code>.nav-tabs</code> class, should <strong>not</strong> be given <code>role=&quot;tablist&quot;</code>, <code>role=&quot;tab&quot;</code> or <code>role=&quot;tabpanel&quot;</code> attributes. These are only appropriate for dynamic tabbed interfaces, as described in the <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/tabpanel/\">ARIA Authoring Practices Guide tabs pattern</a>. See the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/components/tab\">Tab plugin</a> for dynamic tabbed interfaces. The <code>aria-current</code> attribute is not necessary on dynamic tabbed interfaces since our JavaScript handles the selected state by adding <code>aria-selected=&quot;true&quot;</code> on the active tab."},{"id":"using-menus","type":"heading","en":"Using menus","level":2},{"id":"using-menus--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Add menus with a little extra HTML and the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/components/menus#usage\">menus JavaScript plugin</a>."},{"id":"tabs-with-menus","type":"heading","en":"Tabs with menus","level":3},{"id":"tabs-with-menus--example-1","type":"demo","key":"46558b5f8cfd199f5e32","height":147},{"id":"tabs-with-menus--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\" role=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Menu</a>\n    <div class=\"menu\">\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Action</a>\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Another action</a>\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Something else here</a>\n      <hr class=\"menu-divider\">\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Separated link</a>\n    </div>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"pills-with-menus","type":"heading","en":"Pills with menus","level":3},{"id":"pills-with-menus--example-1","type":"demo","key":"ac2558962d0db6565ce3","height":147},{"id":"pills-with-menus--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"nav nav-pills\">\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link active\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Active</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\" role=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Menu</a>\n    <div class=\"menu\">\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Action</a>\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Another action</a>\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Something else here</a>\n      <hr class=\"menu-divider\">\n      <a class=\"menu-item\" href=\"#\">Separated link</a>\n    </div>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"#\">Link</a>\n  </li>\n  <li class=\"nav-item\">\n    <a class=\"nav-link disabled\" aria-disabled=\"true\">Disabled</a>\n  </li>\n</ul>","language":""},{"id":"css","type":"heading","en":"CSS","level":2},{"id":"variables","type":"heading","en":"Variables","level":3},{"id":"variables--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Navs use local CSS variables on <code>.nav</code> for real-time customization. Values for the CSS variables are generated from Sass maps unique to each component and applied to the aforementioned class."},{"id":"variables--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"On the <code>.nav</code> base class:"},{"id":"variables--code-1","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable-next-line scss/dollar-variable-default\n$nav-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --nav-gap: .125rem,\n    --nav-link-gap: .5rem,\n    --nav-link-align: center,\n    --nav-link-justify: center,\n    --nav-link-padding-x: .75rem,\n    --nav-link-padding-y: .375rem,\n    --nav-link-color: var(--fg-2),\n    --nav-link-hover-color: var(--fg-1),\n    --nav-link-hover-bg: var(--bg-1),\n    --nav-link-active-color: var(--fg-body),\n    --nav-link-active-bg: var(--bg-2),\n    --nav-link-disabled-color: var(--fg-4),\n    --nav-link-border-width: var(--border-width),\n    --nav-link-transition-property: \"color, background-color, border-color\",\n    --nav-link-transition-duration: .15s,\n    --nav-link-transition-timing: ease-in-out,\n  ),\n  $nav-tokens\n);","language":""},{"id":"variables--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"On the <code>.nav-tabs</code> modifier class:"},{"id":"variables--code-2","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable-next-line scss/dollar-variable-default\n$nav-tabs-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --nav-tabs-border-width: var(--border-width),\n    --nav-tabs-border-color: var(--border-color),\n    --nav-tabs-border-radius: var(--radius-5),\n    --nav-tabs-link-hover-border-color: var(--border-subtle),\n    --nav-tabs-link-active-color: var(--fg-body),\n    --nav-tabs-link-active-bg: var(--bg-body),\n    --nav-tabs-link-active-border-color: var(--border-color) var(--border-color) var(--bg-body),\n  ),\n  $nav-tabs-tokens\n);","language":""},{"id":"variables--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"On the <code>.nav-pills</code> modifier class:"},{"id":"variables--code-3","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable-next-line scss/dollar-variable-default\n$nav-pills-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --nav-pills-bg: var(--bg-1),\n    --nav-pills-padding: .25rem,\n    --nav-pills-border-radius: 3rem,\n    --nav-pills-link-active-color: var(--primary-contrast),\n    --nav-pills-link-active-bg: var(--primary-bg),\n    --nav-pills-link-border-radius: 3rem,\n  ),\n  $nav-pills-tokens\n);","language":""},{"id":"variables--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"On the <code>.nav-underline</code> modifier class:"},{"id":"variables--code-4","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable-next-line scss/dollar-variable-default\n$nav-underline-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --nav-gap: 1rem,\n    --nav-link-active-bg: transparent,\n    --nav-underline-border-width: .125rem,\n    --nav-underline-link-active-color: var(--fg-body),\n  ),\n  $nav-underline-tokens\n);","language":""}],"demos":[{"key":"005c671d6cae866c649c","html":"<ul class=\"nav\">\n  <li class=\"nav-it